39535021 true] [17592186115675 1145 "Use the product rule $(u\\mathbf f)'=u'\\mathbf f+u\\mathbf f'$. Here $u'=2t$ and $\\mathbf f'=\\langle\\cos t,2,5^t\\ln5\\rangle$, so $$(u\\mathbf f)'=\\begin{bmatrix}2t\\sin t+t^2\\cos t\\\\2t(2t-8)+2t^2\\\\2t5^t+t^25^t\\ln5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}t^2\\cos t+2t\\sin t\\\\6t^2-16t\\\\5^tt^2\\ln5+2t5^t\\end{bmatrix}.$$" 13194139535021 false] [17592186115675 1145 "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({5}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+2t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2{t}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535021 true] [17592186115685 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535021 true] [17592186115685 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535021 false] [17592186115685 1100 "If $\\mathbf f(u)=\\cos u\\,\\mathbf i+(1-u^2)\\mathbf j+12\\mathbf k$ and $u(t)=t^3$, find $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)$." 13194139535021 false] [17592186115685 1100 "If $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,i+(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+12\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" 13194139535021 true] [17592186115685 1145 "Differentiate the outer function: $\\mathbf f'(u)=-\\sin u\\,\\mathbf i-2u\\mathbf j$. The inner derivative is $u'(t)=3t^2$. Therefore $$(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)=(-\\sin(t^3)\\mathbf i-2t^3\\mathbf j)3t^2=-3t^2\\sin(t^3)\\mathbf i-6t^5\\mathbf j.$$" 13194139535021 false] [17592186115685 1145 "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(12)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t))\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t))\\,i-2(u(t))\\,j)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})\\,i-2({t}^{3})\\,j)\\cdot 3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535021 true] [17592186115686 1017 #edb/ref 17592186113516 13194139535021 false] [17592186115686 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327307 13194139535021 true] [17592186115686 1100 "Differentiate $\\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where $$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f(t)&=\\langle3t-1,6-t,7t\\rangle,\\\\\\mathbf g(t)&=\\langle t^2,1-t^2,t\\rangle.\\end{aligned}$$" 13194139535021 false] [17592186115686 1100 "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535021 true] [17592186115686 1145 "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535021 true] [17592186115686 1145 "Differentiate component by component: $\\mathbf f'(t)=\\langle3,-1,7\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle2t,-2t,1\\rangle$. By the sum rule, $$(\\mathbf f+\\mathbf g)'(t)=\\langle2t+3,-2t-1,8\\rangle.$$" 13194139535021 false] [17592186327237 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327238 13194139535021 true] [17592186327237 1089 "q-128473" 13194139535021 true] [17592186327237 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535021 true] [17592186327237 1100 "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" 13194139535021 true] [17592186327237 1113 #uuid "ed124114-d5b6-5cba-b3bb-b981a963c3d5" 13194139535021 true] [17592186327237 1145 "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}\\opera